    double difference = PURCHASE_PRICE - RESIDUAL_VALUE;
    double percentageOfRefund = (REFUND_AMOUNT / difference) * 100;
    std::cout << "The percentage of refund is: " << std::fixed << std::setprecision(2) << percentageOfRefund << "%" << std::endl;
    return 0;
}
```

In addition to the right to a refund as described above, the Consumer Rights Act of 2015 also provides consumers with several other protections:

- The right to receive goods that are of satisfactory quality, fit for purpose, and as described.
- The right to receive goods that match any samples or models shown.
- The right to receive goods that are installed correctly and are supplied with any necessary parts or accessories.
- The right to be informed about the price of the goods, any additional charges, and the total cost before buying.
- The right to have the goods delivered within the agreed timescale, unless there are exceptional circumstances preventing delivery.
- The right to be able to cancel the order

