Here's an example of how you could create a socket for a specific chatroom using PHP and Socket.io:

Assuming your database connection is already set up in the `db_connect.php` file provided, you can create a new file called `chatroom.php` to handle the socket connections for a specific chatroom. Here's some sample code that demonstrates how to do this:

```php
<?php
require_once __DIR__ . '/db_connect.php'; // include the database connection

// load the Socket.io library
require_once __DIR__ . '/socket.io/socket.io.php';

// initialize the Socket.io server
$socket = new \SocketIO\Server(80);

// connect to the database and get the specified chatroom ID
$stmt = $conn->prepare("SELECT id FROM chatrooms WHERE user_id = ? AND chatting_id = ? LIMIT 1");
$stmt->bind_param('ss', $_SESSION['user_id'], $_GET['chatroom']);
$stmt->execute();
$result = $stmt->get_result();
$row = $result->fetch_assoc();
$chatroom_id = $row['id'];

// add event listeners for sending and receiving messages
$socket->on('send-message', function ($data) use ($chatroom_id) {
    $sender_id = $_SESSION['user_id'];
    $message = $data['message'];

    // insert the message into the database
    $stmt = $conn->prepare("INSERT INTO message (chatroom_id, sender_id, message) VALUES (?, ?, ?)");
    $stmt->bind_param('sss', $chatroom_id, $sender_id, $message);
    $stmt->execute();

    // broadcast the message to all connected clients
    $socket->broadcast->to($chatroom_id)->emit('message', ['sender' => $sender_id, 'message' => $message]);
});

// start the Socket.io server
$socket->listen(80);
```

